Two fixes to spin2cpp's P2 optimizer, each a silent miscompile of ordinary code,
both reported upstream with this change as the suggested fix:

flexprop#109 -- two rewrites change the flags a 64-bit add or subtract reads, and
the high word comes out off by one: OptimizeImmediates exchanges ADD and SUB with
a negated immediate (C inverted), and OptimizeAddSub merges two immediate adds,
deleting one whose C or Z is still read. doc/add-immediate-carry.c.

flexprop#110 -- OptimizeReadWrite turns a conditional read of memory into a copy
of an earlier conditional write under the same condition code, although a compare
between the two re-set the flags: `if (a) g ^= K; if (b) g ^= M;` on a global read
a stale register when a was false. doc/conditional-load-dropped.c.

Carried here ahead of upstream: drop each part with the spin2cppRef that carries
a fix of upstream's own.

